  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1012 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nUpper ridging will dominate through late week with the ridge axis \nbeing overhead by Friday afternoon. The upper ridge will be, for a \nlack of a better word, dissolved by the weekend as an upper \nshortwave trough/low quickly pushes across the Desert Southwest to \nthe foothills of the Central Rockies. There is still some \nuncertainty with the potential for precip ahead of this system. The \nGFS is a little more generous than Monday's runs while the ECMWF \nremains the most generous. The overall pattern would still suggest \ndry slotting, but this would still depend mostly on the system being \na progressive open wave trough.",
